WEBVTT

00:00:01.333 --> 00:00:05.167
Registration is essential to humanitarian assistance

00:00:05.167 --> 00:00:07.000
but often faces challenges

00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:09.000
with repeated registrations

00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:10.300
coordination

00:00:10.300 --> 00:00:11.333
overlaps

00:00:11.333 --> 00:00:13.267
and referrals.

00:00:13.267 --> 00:00:14.833
IDEHA

00:00:14.833 --> 00:00:16.900
is working to address this.

00:00:16.900 --> 00:00:19.567
By setting standards for how registration data

00:00:19.567 --> 00:00:22.633
is gathered, exchanged and governed

00:00:22.633 --> 00:00:25.900
organizations can better coordinate assistance

00:00:25.900 --> 00:00:27.600
understand vulnerability

00:00:27.600 --> 00:00:30.633
and provide system-wide referral.

00:00:30.633 --> 00:00:33.433
This federated approach keeps organizations

00:00:33.433 --> 00:00:35.833
in control of data they collect

00:00:35.833 --> 00:00:37.667
yet ensures that it supports

00:00:37.667 --> 00:00:39.900
the wider response.

00:00:39.900 --> 00:00:40.967
To learn more

00:00:40.967 --> 00:00:49.567
visit interoperabledata.xyz
